1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,486
Hello!

2
00:00:00,486 --> 00:00:05,182
Today we'll set up a '모임' [mo-im] (gathering) with several people.

3
00:00:05,182 --> 00:00:08,420
First we have to match everyone's times.

4
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:17,697
Three keys: '약속을 잡다' [yak-sso-geul jap-tta] (set up an appointment),

5
00:00:17,697 --> 00:00:23,730
'시간 조율' [si-gan jo-yul] (coordinate times), '모임' [mo-im] (a gathering).

6
00:00:28,210 --> 00:00:31,901
With more people, every '일정' [il-jeong] (schedule) differs.

7
00:00:31,901 --> 00:00:34,362
Like that rippling flower field,

8
00:00:34,362 --> 00:00:36,900
each is free at a different time.

9
00:00:40,370 --> 00:00:49,608
So you need '조율' [jo-yul] (coordination) — fitting different schedules into one.

10
00:00:49,608 --> 00:00:52,080
Noun 조율, verb 조율하다.

11
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:57,572
Simple order: suggest, coordinate, confirm.

12
00:00:57,572 --> 00:01:03,900
Last time's '할 계획이에요' [hal gye-hoe-gi-e-yo] (I plan to) becomes today's '약속을 잡다' [yak-sso-geul jap-tta].

13
00:01:09,610 --> 00:01:11,796
Now the words — seven today,

14
00:01:11,796 --> 00:01:16,090
and every one of them serves a single '모임' [mo-im] (gathering).

15
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:26,963
'약속' [yak-ssok] (appointment) is a noun — what you agreed to do: 약속이 있어요,

16
00:01:26,963 --> 00:01:29,770
약속을 지켜요. Repeat after me.

17
00:01:33,670 --> 00:01:40,950
'약속을 잡다' [yak-sso-geul jap-tta] means to set the appointment; '잡다' [jap-tta] is the verb.

18
00:01:40,950 --> 00:01:45,240
친구와 저녁 약속을 잡았어요 [chin-gu-wa jeo-nyeok yak-sso-geul ja-ba-sseo-yo]. Repeat after me.

19
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:52,789
'시간 조율' [si-gan jo-yul] means settling a time that fits everyone.

20
00:01:52,789 --> 00:01:56,250
다 같이 시간 조율이 필요해요 [da ga-chi si-gan jo-yu-ri pi-ryo-hae-yo]. Repeat after me.

21
00:01:59,340 --> 00:02:03,964
'모임' [mo-im] (gathering) is people coming together.

22
00:02:03,964 --> 00:02:07,620
금요일에 동아리 모임이 있어요 [geu-myo-i-re dong-a-ri mo-i-mi i-sseo-yo]. Repeat after me.

23
00:02:10,850 --> 00:02:16,180
'회식' [hoe-sik] (company dinner) is coworkers eating together.

24
00:02:16,180 --> 00:02:19,420
다음 주에 회식이 있어요 [da-eum ju-e hoe-si-gi i-sseo-yo]. Repeat after me.

25
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:28,211
'장소' [jang-so] (place) is where you meet: 장소를 정해요, 장소가 어디예요 [jang-so-reul jeong-hae-yo jang-so-ga eo-di-ye-yo].

26
00:02:28,211 --> 00:02:32,780
Easy to find is best. Repeat after me.

27
00:02:36,710 --> 00:02:41,080
'시간 정하다' [si-gan jeong-ha-da] (to decide the time) settles what hour you meet.

28
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:43,763
Set the time and the place follows.

29
00:02:43,763 --> 00:02:44,990
Repeat after me.

30
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:53,272
Now let's do '시간 조율' [si-gan jo-yul] (coordinating times) aloud.

31
00:02:53,272 --> 00:02:57,164
Like that coaster, the talk moves in order: ask,

32
00:02:57,164 --> 00:02:58,380
answer, decide.

33
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:07,775
Start with a question: '언제가 괜찮으세요? [eon-je-ga gwaen-cha-neu-se-yo]

34
00:03:07,775 --> 00:03:09,636
' (When works for you?

35
00:03:09,636 --> 00:03:13,780
) It asks their easy time first. Repeat after me.

36
00:03:16,850 --> 00:03:18,305
To ask gently,

37
00:03:18,305 --> 00:03:23,604
add '혹시' [hok-ssi] (by any chance) in front — it's an adverb.

38
00:03:23,604 --> 00:03:25,370
혹시 토요일 오후에 괜찮으세요? [hok-ssi to-yo-il o-hu-e gwaen-cha-neu-se-yo]

39
00:03:28,220 --> 00:03:31,013
'조율' [jo-yul] (coordination) is never rushed.

40
00:03:31,013 --> 00:03:33,961
Like that panda chewing bamboo slowly,

41
00:03:33,961 --> 00:03:35,900
ask one person at a time.

42
00:03:38,530 --> 00:03:45,983
Ask each person their '가능한 시간' [ga-neung-han si-gan] (available time) — by phone or message.

43
00:03:45,983 --> 00:03:47,580
가능한 시간을 알려 주세요 [ga-neung-han si-ga-neul al-lyeo ju-se-yo].

44
00:03:50,810 --> 00:03:53,099
If your time is open,

45
00:03:53,099 --> 00:03:56,915
answer '언제든 괜찮아요' [eon-je-deun gwaen-cha-na-yo] (any time works).

46
00:03:56,915 --> 00:04:00,840
'언제든' [eon-je-deun] is an adverb. Repeat after me.

47
00:04:03,140 --> 00:04:05,212
For a day that won't work,

48
00:04:05,212 --> 00:04:09,835
soften it: '어려울 것 같아요' [eo-ryeo-ul geot ga-ta-yo] (that may be hard) beats a flat no.

49
00:04:09,835 --> 00:04:11,110
Repeat after me.

50
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:18,996
Refusing alone stalls things. '어떠세요?

51
00:04:18,996 --> 00:04:20,648
' (how about it?

52
00:04:20,648 --> 00:04:25,190
) asks their opinion politely: 일요일 오전은 어떠세요? [i-ryo-il o-jeo-neun eo-tteo-se-yo]

53
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:29,323
The time is set — now the '장소' [jang-so] (place).

54
00:04:29,323 --> 00:04:31,967
Easy to spot like that carousel,

55
00:04:31,967 --> 00:04:33,950
easy for anyone to find.

56
00:04:39,490 --> 00:04:46,703
Add '에서 만나요' [e-seo man-na-yo] (let's meet at) after the place: '카페에서 만나요 [ka-pe-e-seo man-na-yo]' [ka-pe-e-seo man-na-yo],

57
00:04:46,703 --> 00:04:50,120
'역에서 만나요 [yeo-ge-seo man-na-yo]' [yeo-ge-seo man-na-yo]. Repeat after me.

58
00:04:54,600 --> 00:05:01,710
Name an easy landmark: '정문 앞에서 만나요 [jeong-mun a-pe-seo man-na-yo]' [jeong-mun a-pe-seo man-na-yo] (meet in front of the main gate).

59
00:05:01,710 --> 00:05:04,080
'앞에서' [a-pe-seo] tells them where.

60
00:05:05,030 --> 00:05:08,998
To suggest, use '우리 같이 갈래요?

61
00:05:08,998 --> 00:05:12,967
' (shall we go together?).

62
00:05:12,967 --> 00:05:19,140
'같이' [ga-chi] is an adverb; -(으)ㄹ래요 softly invites.

63
00:05:19,590 --> 00:05:21,457
Time and place have met,

64
00:05:21,457 --> 00:05:24,023
so now comes '확정' [hwak-jjeong] (confirmation).

65
00:05:24,023 --> 00:05:26,746
Like that wheel finishing its turn,

66
00:05:26,746 --> 00:05:27,990
the talk closes.

67
00:05:32,880 --> 00:05:34,410
Once you agree,

68
00:05:34,410 --> 00:05:38,795
close with '만나기로 해요' [man-na-gi-ro hae-yo] (let's agree to meet).

69
00:05:38,795 --> 00:05:43,180
-기로 하다 = decided together. Repeat after me.

70
00:05:45,830 --> 00:05:52,893
One last line: '그럼 그렇게 해요 [geu-reom geu-reo-ke hae-yo]' [geu-reom geu-reo-ke hae-yo] (then let's do that) signals it's locked.

71
00:05:52,893 --> 00:05:56,320
Add 미리 예약해 둘게요 — I'll book ahead.

72
00:05:56,770 --> 00:05:59,549
Now for real. On this parade route,

73
00:05:59,549 --> 00:06:04,710
hear three people set up a '모임' [mo-im] (gathering) from start to finish.

74
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:11,565
First, someone asks '모임 어때요?

75
00:06:11,565 --> 00:06:14,748
' (how about a meetup?).

76
00:06:14,748 --> 00:06:18,440
Answer: 좋아요, 시간 조율해서 약속을 잡아요.

77
00:06:20,790 --> 00:06:22,352
Second: '언제가 괜찮으세요? [eon-je-ga gwaen-cha-neu-se-yo]

78
00:06:22,352 --> 00:06:24,902
' One is free Saturday morning,

79
00:06:24,902 --> 00:06:29,260
the other only evening — so move to Sunday afternoon.

80
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:37,540
Third: the time is set, so pick the place.

81
00:06:37,540 --> 00:06:43,300
'정문 앞에서 만나요 [jeong-mun a-pe-seo man-na-yo]' [jeong-mun a-pe-seo man-na-yo] — and the reply, '그럼 그렇게 해요' [geu-reom geu-reo-ke hae-yo]. Done.

82
00:06:45,930 --> 00:06:46,799
Your turn.

83
00:06:46,799 --> 00:06:51,144
Ask politely, give your '가능한 시간' [ga-neung-han si-gan] (available time),

84
00:06:51,144 --> 00:06:54,620
soften the days that fail, then confirm.

85
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:04,027
Korea has '회식' [hoe-sik] (company dinner) — coworkers sharing a meal.

86
00:07:04,027 --> 00:07:08,150
The date is usually coordinated in a group chat.

87
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:16,671
Etiquette: don't just refuse — offer one time that works.

88
00:07:16,671 --> 00:07:21,150
Now fill the blanks with '시간 조율' [si-gan jo-yul] and '약속을 잡다' [yak-sso-geul jap-tta].

89
00:07:26,070 --> 00:07:29,329
Recap: '약속을 잡다' [yak-sso-geul jap-tta], 시간 조율, 모임.

90
00:07:29,329 --> 00:07:35,847
Last lesson's travel-plans video makes it even easier.

91
00:07:35,847 --> 00:07:38,020
See you next time!

